    cautions: [
        'The histories of the individual signs given here come from the secondary literature as the research for this page reported it, and could not be checked against the editions named (Jones, Berthelot, Maunder and the rest). Read them as reports. The Unicode names, code points and version dates were checked and are safe.',
        'Every sign is shown in its modern standard shape. None is presented as Agrippa’s, a manuscript’s or a papyrus’s form, and no “earliest form” is drawn, because none was seen.',
        'Agrippa’s chapter numbers and titles are given from the 1651 English as reported, and are to be checked against the 1533 scan and the 1651 printing.',
        'Geomantic zodiac attributions are left out on purpose: they differ between Agrippa, the geomancy ascribed to Gerard of Cremona and later tables, and no one table should be presented as Agrippa’s.',
        'Unicode names Venus FEMALE SIGN and Mars MALE SIGN, and spells Scorpio SCORPIUS; the page uses the planet and sign names. Uranus, Neptune and Pluto are modern signs and outside this page.',
    ],
